# Button contrast

- Verify the normal, hover, disabled, and selected states of every new or edited button, badge, and action chip in Dark, Light, and Grey themes.
- Never pair `bg-accent` with `text-white` by default. RapidRAW's Dark theme has a white accent, so this can produce white text on a white background.
- Use the shared `Button` component for standard primary actions; it supplies the theme's `text-button-text` foreground.
- For bespoke controls, use a foreground with guaranteed contrast (for example `text-button-text` with a themed background, or an explicit reviewed foreground/background pair).
- Check text-bearing badges as carefully as buttons; they must not become blank-looking pills in any theme.
